    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Only `AcceptanceTest` is a runnable test class (the other two files are the base harness and audit-log capture helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejecting owner creation when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing duplicate-telephone/household pattern:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (new, in `rest/advice/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the `email` field name, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler(DuplicateEmailException.class)` that returns `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` with an `errors` array naming the offending field.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the email (which already lower-cases it), it now calls a new `requireUniqueEmail(...)` helper that compares the incoming lower-cased email against every existing owner's email (trimmed + lower-cased, null-safe) and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a collision.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
